# How the three example pages here are drawn. Checked by
# lasermade-tools/repro-svg.py; $OUT is where the file must be written.
#
# THEY WERE STALE, and this directory is exempted from doc-audit's orphan check
# as "generated" -- a declaration that something generates them, which nothing
# did. Redrawing all three on 2026-09-10 found the same fault as the ten pages
# under coil/search: one sentence of comment inside viewer.py's own template,
# changed under them and never carried through. Invisible on the page.
#
# TWO OF THE THREE TITLES DO NOT DESCRIBE WHAT THEY DRAW, and that is left for
# the author rather than guessed at here:
#
#   three_block_example  titled "D R1 F, the three-block example". D R1 F is not
#                        a walk -- R and F are not letters this notation has, the
#                        same dead spelling that was in bore_split.py's own usage
#                        block until today -- and the page draws D2 E4 N1,
#                        which is eight blocks in two pieces.
#   test_bore            titled "The nine-block test bore". It drew U1 E2 S2 U3
#                        while regress.py gated U2 E2 S2 U2 under the same name
#                        -- both nine blocks, not the same walk. Settled on
#                        2026-09-15: the test bore is U1 E3 S3 U1, nine blocks
#                        in three bends, and both places draw it.
#
# The titles are reproduced here exactly as they ship, so this gate asserts only
# that the pages are what the code draws. Correcting a title means changing the
# line below with it.
notation_example.html :: ~/Software/boxes/venv/bin/python ../viewer.py "E2 S3 U2 N2" --out $OUT --title "The notation worked through"
test_bore.html :: ~/Software/boxes/venv/bin/python ../viewer.py "U1 E3 S3 U1" --out $OUT --title "The nine-block test bore"
three_block_example.html :: ~/Software/boxes/venv/bin/python ../viewer.py "D2 E4 N1" --out $OUT --title "D R1 F, the three-block example"
